<title>USA: Kmart denies signing contract with Chancellor.</title>
<headline>Kmart denies signing contract with Chancellor.</headline>
<dateline>TROY, Mich. 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kmart Corp on Tuesday denied that it signed a contract to sell 15 Builders Square stores to Chancellor Corp, as announced by Chancellor in a release.</p>
<p>Kmart has asked Chancellor to retract the statement, issued on Tuesday morning.</p>
<p>Chancellor officials were unavailable for comment.</p>
<p>Builders Square, owned by Kmart, operates 168 home-improvement centers in the United States.</p>
<p>Chancellor buys investment-grade commercial real estate projects.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
</text>
